<%#
  ONE SHELF (2026-10-20): a folder inside every project, Projects/<project>/<name>/. Its name, the
  extensions that file into it as chips, an "Edit extensions" control, and the shelf's own settings --
  how its panel opens on a project page and which group it sits in. This was the Filing page's
  folder card (stage 4, S4-2; story 4.3) and keeps every class it had.

  THE CHIPS ARE PLAIN UNTIL THE SHELF IS BEING EDITED (UX audit F7). Each chip drew its own red
  "Remove" -- fifty of them on the code shelf, none naming its extension. Now one "Edit extensions"
  per card (a `details`, so it opens by keyboard and says whether it is open) reveals each chip's
  remove button, whose accessible name is "Remove .stl", and the add form. The remove forms are always
  in the page; pages/settings.css hides them while the card's `details` is closed. A refused add
  opens it again, with the error and the typed extension (UX audit B3).

  MOVING `.dxf` FROM design TO laser is a remove on one card and an add on the other -- two clicks on
  a rare action, where a folder picker per chip would put a select on all 124 of them, and a
  free-text folder field per chip is what made "dsign" a real, silent outcome on the flat page this
  replaced. Creating a NEW shelf is the name field at the foot of the page.

  NO RENAME AND NO REMOVE ON `other`: a name is a folder on disk in every project, and `other` is
  where an extension with no shelf files (Settings::ShelvesController#destroy refuses it too).

  Locals: shelf (a Maker::Shelf), by_folder (folder name to its rules, grouped once by
  Settings::ShelvesPage -- a `where` here would be a query per card), groups (the user's groups, for
  the Group menu), level (2 for a shelf in no group, 3 under a group's h2), failed_shelf and new_rule
  (a refused update of a shelf, a refused added extension; nil when nothing was refused).
%>
<% saved = shelf %>
<% shelf = failed_shelf if failed_shelf&.id == saved.id %>
<% adding = new_rule if new_rule&.folder == saved.name %>
<section class="filing-card shelf-card">
  <div class="shelf-card-head">
    <%= content_tag(level == 3 ? :h3 : :h2, "#{saved.name}/", class: "filing-folder mono") %>
    <% unless saved.fallback? %>
      <%= button_to "Remove shelf", settings_shelf_path(saved), method: :delete,
                    class: "linkbtn danger small",
                    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove the #{saved.name}/ shelf? " \
                                                    "Its extensions will file into other." } } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% rules = by_folder[saved.name] || [] %>
  <ul class="filing-exts">
    <% rules.each do |rule| %>
      <li class="chip filing-chip">
        <span class="mono">.<%= rule.ext %></span>
        <%= button_to settings_filing_rule_path(rule), method: :delete,
                      class: "linkbtn danger filing-chip-remove",
                      title: "Remove .#{rule.ext}", "aria-label": "Remove .#{rule.ext}",
                      form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove .#{rule.ext} from the #{saved.name}/ shelf? " \
                                                      "It will file into other until you add it to a shelf again." } } do %>
          <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
        <% end %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
    <% if rules.empty? %>
      <li class="empty inline">Nothing files here yet.</li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <details class="shelf-exts-edit"<%= " open" if adding %>>
    <summary class="linkbtn small">Edit extensions</summary>
    <% if adding %>
      <div class="form-errors" role="alert">Could not add .<%= adding.ext %>:
        <%= adding.errors.full_messages.to_sentence.chomp(".") %>.</div>
    <% end %>
    <%# scope: :filing_rule names the params at all (this form has no model object), which is what
        Settings::FilingRulesController#create requires -- CLAUDE.md's form-scope rule, asserted on
        the RENDERED field names in settings_shelves_test.rb. The folder rides as a hidden field so
        adding an extension to this card is one text box. Both values are stated: with no model the
        fields would otherwise read @filing_rule.

        id: nil ON EVERY FIELD IN THIS CARD. There is one of each form per CARD, and form_with derives
        an id from the scope alone -- so the default spelling puts a dozen elements with id
        "filing_rule_ext" (or "shelf_default_view") on one page, which is invalid HTML and hands
        getElementById an arbitrary one of them. Each label WRAPS its control, so the association is
        implicit and survives having no id at all; the params are unaffected, which is why the
        rendered-field-name assertions still read the same. %>
    <%= form_with url: settings_filing_rules_path, scope: :filing_rule, class: "settings-add filing-add" do |f| %>
      <%= f.hidden_field :folder, value: saved.name, id: nil %>
      <label class="field">
        <span>Add extension</span>
        <%= f.text_field :ext, value: adding&.ext, required: true, placeholder: "lbrn", id: nil %>
      </label>
      <%= f.submit "Add", class: "btn ghost small" %>
    <% end %>
  </details>
  <% if shelf.errors.any? %>
    <div class="form-errors" role="alert">Could not save <%= saved.name %>/:
      <%= shelf.errors.full_messages.to_sentence.chomp(".") %>.</div>
  <% end %>
  <%# scope: :shelf is what Settings::ShelvesController#update requires. A namespaced model scopes
      to maker_shelf on its own, which that action would refuse as a missing param (section 14d).
      The model is the refused shelf after a refusal, so its selects keep what was chosen. %>
  <%= form_with model: shelf, url: settings_shelf_path(saved), scope: :shelf, method: :patch,
                class: "shelf-settings" do |f| %>
    <label class="field">
      <span>View</span>
      <%= f.select :default_view,
                   [ [ "Automatic", "" ], *Maker::Project::VIEWS.map { |v| [ v.capitalize, v ] } ],
                   {}, id: nil %>
    </label>
    <label class="field">
      <span>Group</span>
      <%= f.select :shelf_group_id, [ [ "None", "" ], *groups.map { |g| [ g.name, g.id ] } ],
                   {}, id: nil %>
    </label>
    <%= f.submit "Save", class: "btn ghost small" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
